From 537bff1e543203eaacac0e5ceea1be3c53674e1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite-Emulator Dev <dev@auralite-emu.local>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 11:34:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] U2 update

USB U2: SCSI enumeration set over the honest BOT channel.

The four commands AuraLite-OS@0ed0d29 drivers/usb/msc.c actually sends
(measured: TUR x5 with REQUEST SENSE retries, INQUIRY allocation 36
with vendor at +8 / product at +16, READ CAPACITY(10) parsed be32 +
be32 and rejected unless 512) are answered from the attached image:

- INQUIRY: 36-byte direct-access (0x00), removable (RMB 0x80), SPC-3,
  RDF-2, vendor 'AURALITE', product 'USB DISK', revision '1.0 '.
- READ CAPACITY(10): last LBA = disk_len/512 - 1, block length 512 --
  pinned at both 1-block and N-block images.
- TEST UNIT READY: OK with an image; FAILED + sense 2/3A (NOT READY /
  MEDIUM NOT PRESENT) without one, and the guest's retry loop reads it
  back via REQUEST SENSE.
- REQUEST SENSE: 18-byte fixed format (0x70, key/ASC/ASCQ, additional
  length 0x0A), consumed on read; the U1 FAILED path saves
  ILLEGAL REQUEST 5/20 for unsupported opcodes.

tests/test_usb.c grows 7 -> 14 machine vectors: ok tur ready,
ok tur no image failed (U2 negative control: FAILED, not OK),
ok request sense not ready (2/3A returned then consumed), ok inquiry
response (36 bytes compared), ok read capacity n-block (8 sectors ->
last LBA 7), ok read capacity 1-block (last LBA 0), ok illegal opcode
sense (5/20).

Once-per-phase negative control (measured): breaking the capacity math
(disk_len/512 without the -1) reddens exactly ok read capacity n-block
(assert r[3] == 7).

READ(10)/READ(12) keep the U1 channel; firmware receipts byte-stable
(make test boot gate green).

Gate: make test + make test-sanitize green; docs synced (USB_PLAN U2
receipts, CHANGELOG 0038, ROADMAP queue).
